Chapter: Exception Test Deep Frames

 A fault raised several frames down, so the exception dump's frame walk
 has a chain to follow. The other exc- samples fault immediately out of
 opening, which leaves one frame at the very top of RAM, and the dump
 switches RSP to that same top and pushes over it before it can be read.
 A deep fault puts the frames well below anything the handler touches.

 The recursion is deliberately not a tail call: `descend (n - 1) + n`
 keeps a live use after the call, so each level owns a real frame. A
 tail call would be a jmp and the whole chain would collapse into one
 activation. The parameter count and the arithmetic after the call are
 also what keep the frontend's cost-based inliner from eating the
 function before any of this is emitted.

Section: Body
  descend : Integer -> Integer
  descend (n) =
   if n <= 0 then peek-qword 4294967296 0
   else descend (n - 1) + n

  opening : Integer = descend 6

